============================================================================
WHAT THE BAND WAS TAKEN TO SHOW, AND WHAT SURVIVES
============================================================================
  the registry's reading: the band sits 2.2% below 3.alpha, so P-2026-040
  is a bet against a running instrument rather than a fit. That framing is sound --
  registering against an unconverged chain is legitimate PRE-REGISTRATION.

  What is not sound is using the same band as a CONSTRAINT, which later work did:
    - 'd = 3 is excluded at every scale' rested on the band's top being below 3.alpha;
    - the three-way conflict on d counted the band as one of its three constraints.
  Both inherit R-1 = 93 and neither survives it.

============================================================================
THE d PICTURE WITH THE BAND WITHDRAWN
============================================================================
  constraint                                       d
  ----------------------------------------------------
  the spatial dimension (theory)              3.0000
  the observed dark-energy density            2.9934
  the hierarchy anchor exact landing          2.9211
  the indirect band                        WITHDRAWN

  Theory and observation agree to 0.22% -- which is the floor's recorded
  +0.44%, since rho goes as d^2. The anchor sits 2.63% below both.

  So there is no three-way conflict. There is the single exposure section 6f already
  named: the anchor's exact landing wants a coupling weaker than the infrared limit,
  and cannot have it at any scale. Removing the band does not weaken the corpus --
  it removes an apparent second constraint that was never entitled to the name, and
  leaves the picture simpler and better than the three-way reading described.
